      "text": "The import `from qiskit.aqua.operators.legacy import commutator` is the bug. That function was written only for Aqua's legacy Pauli operators, such as `WeightedPauliOperator`. It cannot accept a `DensityMatrix`, an `Operator`, or a raw NumPy array, which is why every input type raises the same error. Aqua has also since been removed from Qiskit.\n\nThe fix replaces that import with a small `commutator` that computes `[A, B] = AB − BA` using `qiskit.quantum_info.Operator`. The call `commutator(dm0, dm1)` is left as it was.\n\n```python\nfrom qiskit import QuantumCircuit\nfrom qiskit.quantum_info import DensityMatrix\n# FIX: aqua legacy commutator only accepts legacy Pauli operators (and aqua is removed) -> define commutator via quantum_info Operator, because it must compute AB - BA for matrix-like inputs such as DensityMatrix\nfrom qiskit.quantum_info import Operator\ndef commutator(a, b):\n    A = Operator(a.data)\n    B = Operator(b.data)\n    return A.dot(B) - B.dot(A)\n\ncirc0 = QuantumCircuit(1)\ncirc1 = QuantumCircuit(1)\n\ncirc0.x(0)\ndm0 = DensityMatrix.from_instruction(circ0)\n\ncirc1.z(0)\ndm1 = DensityMatrix.from_instruction(circ1)\n\ncommutator(dm0, dm1)\n\n```",
